(1)
Where a Declaration of Performance and Conformity is issued in relation to a product not subject to product requirements 
established by delegated acts referred to in Article 7(1), points 10 and 11(c) are omitted.
(2)
Only one unique, unequivocal declaration code per product type shall be used, even where there are variants, variants being 
variations of the product type that do not influence performance or conformity of the product.
(3)
Different versions may be issued, e.g. to correct mistakes or add complementary information.
